    fix(AUG-045): enforce declared primary key on table POST — reject rows missing/null pk with 400
    
    A row inserted without the declared primary key value was stored with
    pk:null and became unreachable (PATCH/DELETE require ?pk=eq.<value>),
    leaving hand-editing the JSONL as the only escape. The POST /:table
    route now validates, AFTER coercion and BEFORE any writer enqueue or
    legacy append, that every row carries a non-null, non-empty primary-key
    value when the table declares one; violations get 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
    and nothing from the batch is inserted. Tables with no declared pk are
    unchanged. The check sits before the storage-path branch, so both the
    schema.json writer path and the legacy appendRowsToTable path enforce it.
    
    Addresses AUG-045.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
